Q37  Q31 netd, 64 slots, still drops on burst                76.79 s = 0.3836 MB/s, input_fail=76
Q38  Q38 netd, 64 slots, waits instead of dropping           34.58 s = 0.8518 MB/s, input_fail=0, input_retry=103

## reading
Removing the software drop more than doubled throughput and removed the retransmission
storm: input_fail 76 -> 0, overlap collapsed, and the phone no longer had to recover a
collapsed congestion window. 103 waits replaced the drops, so the loss was real and it
came from netd, not from the air. The 1.12 MB/s historical best used merge ON and a
social slot; this run still used -j 0, so the next single variable is the merge.
The keep-alive TCP connection again stayed open after the transfer (proxy 2 active=1).
